    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s lineup today, **Bryce Harper** (78.76) stands as our clear anchor, benefiting from a robust 0.390 xwOBA and an impressive historical BvP edge against Alcantara. Pairing him with **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) provides us with high-ceiling production; **Lawrence Butler** finds himself in a prime spot against Lugo, where favorable SP skill metrics and a strong platoon advantage inflate his output well beyond his base projection. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.65) continues to be an automatic start, as his reliability in the #2 hole against Wilkinson provides the stability needed to chase our 5x5 targets. While **Jonathan Aranda** (67.95) faces the tough Scherzer, the matchup remains statistically favorable for our needs, as Aranda\u2019s dynamic platoon edge against right-handed pitching provides the necessary boost to remain a strong start despite the pedigree of the opposing arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Masyn Winn** (46.70), who barely missed the cut. While his speed profile is highly attractive given our need for stolen bases, the optimizer favored the higher daily efficiency scores of our active middle infielders, specifically noting the superior park and platoon dynamics currently working in favor of **Brendan Donovan** (62.56) and **Luis Arraez** (64.88). Elsewhere, **Dylan Beavers** (64.36) is a high-reward play today, boasting a significant +16% park adjustment that makes him a standout against Warren. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (51.35) closely; he sits at the lower end of our active spectrum due to a platoon disadvantage against May, but he remains in the lineup to protect our power categories. We have avoided **Gleyber Torres** (36.78) entirely, as a daunting matchup against Skenes pushes him well below our 40.0 floor for game cap preservation.",
